        "sign_ok4r02": {
          "type": "sign",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Scientists Call Astaxanthin The King Of Antioxidants For A Reason",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/red-algae-lab.jpg",
            "image_alt": "Astaxanthin research dating back to 1938",
            "body": "<p>Astaxanthin was discovered in 1938 by Nobel Prize-winning chemist Richard Kuhn. It has been studied for nearly 90 years and appears across more than 700 peer-reviewed clinical trials.</p><p>Then come the numbers that make ordinary antioxidants look tiny:</p><ul><li><strong>Up to 6,000 times stronger than vitamin C</strong></li><li><strong>800 times stronger than CoQ10</strong></li><li><strong>550 times stronger than vitamin E</strong></li><li><strong>50 times more absorbable than turmeric</strong></li></ul><p>It has also recorded the highest oxygen radical absorbance capacity measured in an antioxidant.</p><p>This is not another fashionable berry powder with a celebrity attached to it. Scientists have been pulling this molecule apart since before World War II.</p>",
            "close_text": "Vitamin C had the fame. CoQ10 had the doctors. Turmeric had the hype. Astaxanthin had the raw power all along.",
            "show_inline_cta": false,
            "inline_cta_text": "",
            "inline_cta_label": "Put the King of Antioxidants on guard",
            "testimonial_1_initial": "",
