        "sign_ok4r03": {
          "type": "sign",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "You Are Not Aging One Body Part At A Time",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/joint-rot-spread-1x1.gif",
            "image_alt": "Oxidative stress affecting the skin, eyes, heart, muscles, and joints",
            "body": "<p>The medical term is oxidative stress. The plain-English term is internal rot. Yes, rot.</p><p>It is the chemical damage created when oxygen, sunlight, stress, pollution, processed food, and normal metabolism produce more free radicals than your body can neutralize.</p><p>That damage does not pick one target and stop. It shows up as skin that looks older than it should. Energy that disappears by mid-afternoon. Eyes that tire after a screen. A heart working against damaged blood vessels. Joints that complain every time you stand.</p><p>Most people chase each symptom with a different bottle because nobody told them the same cellular fire may be burning underneath all of them.</p>",
            "close_text": "You do not need seven disconnected answers for seven aging complaints. You need to protect the cells they all have in common.",
            "show_inline_cta": false,
            "inline_cta_text": "",
            "inline_cta_label": "Put the King of Antioxidants on guard",
            "testimonial_1_initial": "",
            "testimonial_1_text": "",
            "testimonial_1_by": "",
            "testimonial_2_initial": "",
            "testimonial_2_text": "",
