        "sign_ok4r07": {
          "type": "sign",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Inflammation Is The Slow Fire Behind Stiff Mornings And Aching Joints",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/inflamation-vs-astaxanthin.jpg",
            "image_alt": "Inflammation cooling inside knee and shoulder cells",
            "body": "<p>Inflammation is supposed to be an emergency crew. But when oxidative stress keeps pulling the alarm, the crew never leaves.</p><p>That low, constant fire can touch everything from how your hands feel in the morning to how your knees handle stairs and how your shoulders let you sleep.</p><p>In a 2023 randomized controlled trial, participants reported a <strong>55% reduction in pain at eight weeks.</strong></p><p>That helps explain why the joint story is bigger than numbing one sore spot. The goal is to turn down the cellular alarm that keeps calling inflammation back.</p>",
            "close_text": "You are not weak, lazy, or simply old. Your cells may be stuck in an emergency that never ends.",
            "show_inline_cta": false,
            "inline_cta_text": "",
            "inline_cta_label": "Put the King of Antioxidants on guard",
            "testimonial_1_image": "shopify://shop_images/m.jpg",
            "testimonial_1_initial": "G",
            "testimonial_1_text": "I got my husband back.",
            "testimonial_1_by": "Gary's wife, outside Nashville",
            "testimonial_2_image": "shopify://shop_images/s.jpg",
            "testimonial_2_initial": "S",
            "testimonial_2_text": "I'd done the collagen, the turmeric, two different creams. Nothing. About three weeks in, I got down on the floor with my grandson and got right back up. My husband said I seemed like me again.",
            "testimonial_2_by": "Sarah B, 55, Orange, CA",
            "testimonial_3_image": "shopify://shop_images/g.jpg",
            "testimonial_3_initial": "M",
            "testimonial_3_text": "I'd done glucosamine, turmeric, even cortisone shots. Two and a half weeks in, I was sleeping through the night for the first time in months. My wife noticed before I did.",
            "testimonial_3_by": "Mike D, 54",
            "body_after_testimonials": ""
          }
        },
        "sign_ok4r08": {
          "type": "sign",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Your Heart Never Gets A Day Off From Oxidative Stress",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/heart.jpg",
            "image_alt": "Astaxanthin supporting heart cells and microcirculation",
            "body": "<p>Your heart beats roughly 100,000 times a day. Every beat depends on healthy muscle cells, flexible blood vessels, and blood that can move freely through the smallest channels.</p><p>Oxidative stress attacks all three.</p><p>Astaxanthin has been studied for triglycerides, HDL cholesterol, blood flow, microcirculation, and the oxidation of LDL particles involved in plaque formation. The Okinawa story becomes even harder to ignore when you learn Okinawans experience <strong>80% less heart disease than Americans.</strong></p><p>You can feel a sore knee. You cannot feel oxidative damage accumulating in a blood vessel. That is exactly why daily protection matters.</p>",
            "close_text": "The organ working hardest to keep you alive should not be the last one you decide to protect.",
            "show_inline_cta": false,
            "inline_cta_text": "",
            "inline_cta_label": "Put the King of Antioxidants on guard",
