        "sign_ok4r09": {
          "type": "sign",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Astaxanthin Reaches The Tiny Eye Muscles Screens Exhaust Every Day",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/eye-cross-section.jpg",
            "image_alt": "Astaxanthin supporting tired eyes after screen use",
            "body": "<p>Your eyes were not designed for ten straight hours of phones, laptops, LED light, and close-up focus.</p><p>That strain hits the tiny muscles that help your eyes shift focus. It also piles oxidative stress onto some of the most delicate, light-exposed tissue in your body.</p><p>Astaxanthin crosses barriers most antioxidants cannot and accumulates in eye tissue. Multiple randomized trials report improvements in eye fatigue, visual acuity, and the ability to refocus at different distances.</p><p>That means fewer evenings rubbing tired eyes, fewer moments waiting for the page to sharpen, and less of that heavy, gritty feeling after another full day on a screen.</p>",
            "close_text": "Your screen time keeps climbing. Your cellular eye protection should climb with it.",
            "show_inline_cta": false,
